mode: "100644"
text: "# The FOUND framework — rank a pin in Pinterest search\n\nPinterest is a **search engine**, so ranking is keyword + relevance + engagement, not followers. FOUND\nstructures the SEO. The agent **researches the queries + writes the keyworded title/description + specs the\non-pin keyword + advises the board/link**; **WoopSocial publishes the pin's title + description + board +\nlink**; **profile, board setup, alt text, Rich Pins, and the research tools are native/advised.**\n\n## F — Find the real queries\n- **Pinterest autocomplete + Guided Search bubbles + Trends/Predicts.** **Long-tail (3+ words)**; ~97%\n  unbranded; think like a searcher. *The agent advises the method — it can't query Pinterest's tools or\n  fabricate volume.*\n\n## O — Optimize the pin's words\n- **Title:** lead with the primary keyword — `[Keyword] | [Benefit] | [Context]` (≤100). **Description:**\n  natural, keyword-rich, ~100–200 chars, **no stuffing.** These are the **publishable SEO surfaces** (via\n  WoopSocial). Spec the **on-pin overlay keyword** → render in `ideogram` (text-in-image).\n\n## U — Unify Pin → Board → Page\n- The pin, its **semantically-precise board**, and the **destination page** all reinforce the **same keyword\n  phrase.** **Claim the site + enable Rich Pins**; the **link must deliver the pin's promise** (long clicks =\n  top signal).\n\n## N — Nest keywords across every surface\n- **Keyword layering:** profile name/bio (broad) → board titles/descriptions (topic) → pin title/description/\n  alt text/file name (long-tail). *Most are native/advised; WoopSocial publishes the pin's title + description\n  + board + link.*\n\n## D — Deploy fresh, in clusters, on a seasonal clock\n- **Fresh keyword-optimized pins** (not dupes — each a new ranking chance); publish **related clusters**;\n  **seasonal 45–90 days ahead** via Trends; optimize for **saves + long clicks**; compounds over the ~4-month\n  pin life.\n\n## The SEO brief a request should fill\n```\nQUERIES: seed -> autocomplete + Guided Search bubbles + Trends; pick long-tail (3+ words) with intent (method only; no fabricated volume)\nTITLE: [Primary Keyword] | [Benefit] | [Context] (<=100)   DESCRIPTION: natural, keyword-rich, 100-200 chars, no stuffing\nON-PIN: the keyword in the overlay (-> ideogram)            BOARD: semantically precise name (advised; native to set)\nALIGN: Pin -> Board -> Page reinforce one phrase; claimed site + Rich Pins (native); link delivers the promise\nDEPLOY: fresh (not dupes) + clusters + seasonal 45-90 days ahead; optimize for saves + long clicks\nPUBLISH (WoopSocial): title + description + board (pinterestBoardId) + link (<=2048). Rest native/advised; never fabricate volume/rankings.\n```\n"
